---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Terms of Use — TubeTrainer';
const description = 'The terms for using the TubeTrainer app and website, including the fitness disclaimer.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/terms">
  <section class="section prose-page">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p class="lead">
        These terms govern your use of the TubeTrainer iOS app and the tubetrainer.app website. By using
        TubeTrainer, you agree to them. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the app.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p><strong>Not medical advice.</strong> TubeTrainer is a fitness-tracking tool, not a medical device or
        a substitute for professional advice. Exercise carries risk. Consult a qualified physician before
        starting any exercise programme, and stop if you feel unwell. You train at your own risk.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Licence</h2>
      <p>
        We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use TubeTrainer on Apple devices you
        own or control, for your own personal, non-commercial use, in line with the Apple App Store terms and
        the standard Apple Licensed Application End User Licence Agreement (EULA).
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        The workouts, notes, and coaching references you create are yours. They’re stored on your device (see our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>). You’re responsible for keeping your own backups.
      </p>

      <h2>YouTube content</h2>
      <p>
        TubeTrainer lets you save references to, and play, videos hosted on YouTube. That content belongs to its
        respective creators and is provided by YouTube. TubeTrainer does not own, download, host, or redistribute
        it. Your use of YouTube content is subject to the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener" target="_blank">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
        TubeTrainer is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by YouTube or Google.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to misuse the app — for example, by attempting to reverse engineer it (except where
      permitted by law), interfering with its operation, or using it to break the law or any third party’s terms.</p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        TubeTrainer is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, whether express or
        implied, to the fullest extent permitted by law. We don’t guarantee the app will be uninterrupted,
        error-free, or that video content from third parties will always be available.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or
        consequential damages, or for any loss of data, arising from your use of TubeTrainer. Nothing in these
        terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law (such as for death or personal injury caused by
        negligence).
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the app after changes means you accept the
        updated terms. We’ll update the “last updated” date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and any disputes are subject to the
        non-exclusive jurisdiction of its courts.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Need to reach us? See the <a href="/support">Support</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
